# Programs held out of the differential run. One basename per line (no
# extension), each with the reason it is not run; remove an entry once
# that reason no longer holds. A reason that measurement contradicts is
# worse than no entry at all -- it is read as a known cost and stops
# anyone looking.
#
# Nothing is held out. Thirteen of these listings put no page into the
# comparison and every one of them is still rendered, because the entry
# that would keep one out of the run is the entry nothing measures
# again: what each of the thirteen does is written in nopage instead,
# where the claim is checked both ways every run and lapses of its own
# accord the day the program draws. Two of them ask for something that
# is not a page description -- a job that leaves job encapsulation on a
# password, a job that opens a font file for writing -- and what a run
# does with the request is worth reaching as much as a page would be.
